<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Log Aggregation with OpenSearch'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Log Aggregation with AWS OpenSearch</h1>
  <p>Centralized logging using OpenSearch — streamed CloudWatch logs from Lambda for real-time visualization and analysis in Kibana dashboards.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>OpenSearch</span><span>CloudWatch</span><span>Lambda</span><span>DynamoDB</span><span>Kibana</span><span>DevOps</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/opensearch-logs.png" alt="OpenSearch Log Aggregation Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>centralized log aggregation</strong> using Amazon OpenSearch Service, enabling powerful search and visualization of application logs in real-time.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Deployed infrastructure using <strong>CloudFormation</strong> (DynamoDB, Lambda, IAM).</li>
      <li>Generated logs by invoking <strong>Lambda with test events</strong>.</li>
      <li>Created an <strong>OpenSearch cluster</strong> and configured CloudWatch streaming.</li>
      <li>Visualized logs using <strong>OpenSearch Dashboards (Kibana)</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>📥 Log Pipeline</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Lambda</strong> — Processes events, generates logs</li>
          <li><strong>CloudWatch Logs</strong> — Captures Lambda output</li>
          <li><strong>Subscription Filter</strong> — Streams to OpenSearch</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔍 Search & Visualize</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>OpenSearch Service</strong> — Indexes and stores logs</li>
          <li><strong>Kibana Dashboards</strong> — Visualize log patterns</li>
          <li>Index pattern: <code>cwl-*</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🏗️ Infrastructure</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>CloudFormation</strong> — Provisions all resources</li>
          <li><strong>DynamoDB</strong> — Application data store</li>
          <li><strong>IAM</strong> — Cross-service permissions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Implementation Steps</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p>Deployed <strong>CloudFormation stack</strong> (DynamoDB, Lambda, IAM roles).</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p>Invoked Lambda with <strong>PUT test events</strong> to generate logs.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p>Created <strong>OpenSearch domain</strong> (t3.small.search instance).</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p>Set up <strong>CloudWatch subscription filter</strong> to stream logs to OpenSearch.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p>Created <strong>index pattern (cwl-*)</strong> and visualized logs in Discover.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Set up <strong>OpenSearch Service</strong> (managed Elasticsearch) cluster.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>CloudWatch subscription filters</strong> for log parsing and forwarding.</li>
      <li>Created <strong>index patterns</strong> for organizing log data in OpenSearch.</li>
      <li>Understood <strong>IAM permissions</strong> for cross-service log streaming.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

